[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    124[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   sparse alphabet never produces. Dense alphabets with uniform weights were
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    125[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   added so the row genuinely covers it (the test fails if any of opcodes 16, 17,
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    126[0m:[38;5;10m[49m   18 is never emitted).
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    127[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    128[0m:[38;5;10m[49m ### Not comparable: unbounded-copy paths
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    129[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    130[0m:[38;5;10m[49m 1.7 % of the fuzz cases (325 / 19 000) make **both** libraries exceed the 300 ms
[0m[49m[38;5;10m+    131[0m:[38;5;10m[49m per-call watchdog. These are the cases where the `lens[320]` overflow rewrites
